			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> setting aside the moral/ethical issues with LLMs (which you shouldn’t), it seems like there is basically an impossible problem here. in order to allow them to do anything useful, you have to expose them to sensitive information, but it is currently impossible to truly secure them against prompt injection, so you should never expose them to sensitive information.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
